  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROMOTING COMMUNITY POLICING IN IRAQ</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to enhance local police services at the national and local level through the Community Policing (CP) approach, which aims at rebuilding and strengthening trust between members of the public and the police through community engagement. The project seeks to strengthen access to justice and security in Iraq and contribute to the broader SSR 
The project will provide comprehensive technical advisory support to the MoI including specialized local police departments, at the national and local levels. In an effort to foster sustainability and long-term impact, the Project aims to institutionalize the CP model, enhance MoI ownership and rebuild public trust in police departments. Additionally, the project will support the UN Security Resolution 1325 on WPS by by promoting the active role of Iraqi women in security dialogues and the role of female police officers in the security sector. The project also supports the reintegration of Iraqi nationals from NES and addresses P/CVE.</narrative>
  </description>
